TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Confirmed the exact failure predicted by overseer steer 9: checkpoint cp-smoke ran against base 6e818349eeb947501ac04ba83e826764a042011c, which does not contain the stdin fix ae10e94 (`git merge-base --is-ancestor ae10e94 HEAD` exits 1). At that base, scripts/run-smoke.sh line 10 invokes `podman run --rm --device /dev/kfd ...` with no `-i`/`--interactive`, so the `<<'PY'` heredoc never reaches the container's stdin; python3 reads an empty program, runs nothing, and exits 0. The captured stdout is the single line `smoke receipt: .../results/receipts/smoke.json (fail receipts land under results/receipts/failed/)` with no probe JSON at all, and results/receipts/ contains only build.json, weights-coordinator.json and weights-worker.json — no smoke.json under either results/receipts/ or results/receipts/failed/. The trailing validator heredoc in scripts/run-smoke.sh therefore exits 1 because results/receipts/smoke.json is absent, which is the reported exitCode 1. This is not the admission-probe TypeError: the probe fix 7509202 is present in this base and its bare `_supports_quant_scheme` call is intact at scripts/run-smoke.sh, but it is unreachable while no python source is delivered. Not retryable inside this task: cp-smoke is a checkpoint whose argv is fixed by the worklist and which must not modify the repository, and the required edit lives on main at ae10e94 outside this task's authority. The blocker is purely lineage — ae10e94 must enter the proven integration base before any cp-smoke re-run can differ from this attempt.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh","scripts/make-proxy.sh"],"goal":"Carry the podman stdin fix already made on main at ae10e94 into the proven integration lineage as a lane commit, so that checkpoint cp-smoke can execute its heredoc probes at all. The podman run invocation in scripts/run-smoke.sh must pass -i (or --interactive) so the here-document python program is delivered to the container's stdin, and the identical defect in scripts/make-proxy.sh must carry the same flag. Make no other behavioral change: the five probes (arch, fp8_cast, registry, aperture, admission), the boolean-predicate admission call from patches/0008, the receipt-quarantine logic, the receipt-restore purity guard, and the trailing validator must remain exactly as they are at 6e818349eeb947501ac04ba83e826764a042011c. After this task lands in the proven base, cp-smoke should be re-run: the container is expected to print the receipt JSON and land a pass receipt at results/receipts/smoke.json.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"run-smoke-interactive-flag","description":"The podman run invocation that feeds the heredoc in scripts/run-smoke.sh passes an interactive flag so container stdin is attached.","argv":["bash","-c","sed -n '/podman run/,/^PY$/p' scripts/run-smoke.sh | grep -Eq -- '(^|[[:space:]])(-i|-it|--interactive)([[:space:]]|$)'"]},{"id":"make-proxy-interactive-flag","description":"The corresponding podman run invocation in scripts/make-proxy.sh passes the same interactive flag, closing the identical defect before cp-proxy runs.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -Eq -- 'podman run.*(-i|-it|--interactive)([[:space:]]|$)' scripts/make-proxy.sh || sed -n '/podman run/,/^PY$/p' scripts/make-proxy.sh | grep -Eq -- '(^|[[:space:]])(-i|-it|--interactive)([[:space:]]|$)'"]},{"id":"admission-probe-unchanged","description":"The admission probe still calls _supports_quant_scheme as a bare boolean predicate per patches/0008, with no tuple unpack reintroduced.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -q 'ok = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh && grep -q 'boolean predicate (patches/0008)' scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"purity-guard-still-wired","description":"The checkpoint-purity guard scripts/receipt-restore.py remains invoked from scripts/run-smoke.sh so re-runs leave tracked receipts byte-identical.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -q 'receipt-restore.py' scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"smoke-script-syntax-ok","description":"Both edited scripts remain syntactically valid bash.","argv":["bash","-c","bash -n scripts/run-smoke.sh && bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh"]}]}}
